/**
 * @mainpage pprzlink++ C++ API
 *
 * pprzlink++ loads message schemas from XML at runtime. A Message owns its
 * definition and populated values; codecs turn those values into binary or
 * text data, and transports exchange complete messages over a Device, UDP
 * or Ivy. No generated C++ class is needed for each XML message.
 *
 * @section components Components
 * - @ref messages defines schemas, checked values and message addressing.
 * - @ref codecs encodes fields, PPRZLINK v2 frames and Ivy message text.
 * - @ref transports provides byte streams, serial ports, framing and UDP.
 * - @ref xbee provides XBee AP=1 framing and asynchronous AT initialization.
 * - @ref ivy provides an optional independent Ivy bus and scoped subscriptions.
 * - @ref errors describes the exceptions reported by the public API.
 * - @ref internals documents shared validation and payload helpers.
 *
 * The CMake target `pprzlink::core` contains schemas, codecs and compiled LLNL/units conversions;
 * `pprzlink::io` adds operating-system I/O, and `pprzlink::ivy` adds the optional
 * Ivy 3.18+ adapter. The aggregate targets remain available for compatibility.
 *
 * @section lifetimes Ownership and execution
 * Declare MessageDictionary before any object borrowing it. Transports own
 * their Device exclusively. BoostSerialPortDevice and UdpTransport borrow
 * an Asio context that must outlive them. Service the context to progress
 * asynchronous serial reads; calls to one transport must be serialized.
 * Ivy callbacks run on the bus loop and need synchronization when sharing
 * application data with another thread. Keep subscription tokens alive and
 * finish external calls before destroying the objects they use.
 *
 * @section values Values and wire formats
 * A field has no value until populated. Writes perform checked conversion
 * to the XML type. Exact reads use the stored C++ type; numeric conversions
 * must be requested explicitly. Binary frames carry identifiers and values,
 * so both endpoints need compatible XML schemas and field order.
 * getFieldSI()/setFieldSI() request coherent SI conversions with double values.
 * Integer SI writes round to nearest, with ties away from zero, and retain
 * the XML storage type. MessageField exposes original XML unit metadata and
 * the prepared SI unit; UnitAliases.cpp contains editable scoped conventions.
 *
 * @section examples Learning examples
 * The repository's guide_d_utilisation.md walks through the public API.
 * The offline `si_units` example demonstrates metadata, conversion and native framing.
 * The `pty_agent` example runs the same sender/receiver at either end of a
 * virtual serial pair. `link++ -socat start` creates interchangeable ports
 * and `link++ -socat stop` removes them. These utilities are application
 * examples; the library does not impose aircraft discovery or retry policy.
 */

/** @defgroup messages Message schemas and values
 * XML definitions, exact reads, checked conversions and message addressing.
 */
/** @defgroup codecs Binary and text codecs
 * Stateless encoding plus incremental PPRZLINK v2 frame decoding.
 */
/** @defgroup transports Devices and transports
 * Byte-stream contracts, operating-system I/O and UDP messages.
 */
/** @defgroup xbee XBee radio transport
 * AP=1 radio frames, status events, baud detection and AT initialization.
 */
/** @defgroup ivy Ivy bus adapter
 * Independent buses, scoped subscriptions and request/answer helpers.
 */
/** @defgroup errors Exceptions
 * Error categories preserving the standard C++ catch contracts.
 */
/** @defgroup internals Internal helpers
 * Shared validation and payload functions; implementation details rather
 * than an extension interface for application code.
 */

/** @namespace pprzlink
 * @brief C++ message definitions, codecs, byte streams and transport adapters.
 */
/** @namespace pprzlink::binary
 * @brief Little-endian scalar and XML field codecs.
 */
/** @namespace pprzlink::ivy_codec
 * @brief Ivy text serialization, bindings and legacy OCaml-compatible formats.
 */
/** @namespace pprzlink::detail
 * @brief Shared implementation helpers for checked values and wire payloads.
 */
/** @namespace pprzlink::detail::xml
 * @brief XML element, attribute and identifier validation.
 */
